Feature: Keep /sdlc-execute supervising after it stops a stage worker that already settled

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Stopping a settled worker does not crash the controller
    Given a stage subagent that has written its handoff and settled
    When the controller stops it
    Then the stop is confirmed and the controller continues routing without worker_stop_failed

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A resumed controller is supervised in the same session
    Given a controller that exited in a Claude Code session
    When the supervisor runs supervise again in that session and the Bash call is backgrounded
    Then the new controller session receives hooks-module heartbeats and its spawn requests are answered
    And it does not exit supervising_session_lost
